Dear =
Bhumika=
=
,

Get ready for a frightfully fun week filled with events and celebrations in=
cluding the Students' Union Halloween Party in Sult.

This week we are also celebrating Black Legacies Unbound as part of Black H=
istory Month.

Don't forget, the fees payment deadline for semester one is Saturday 31 Oct=
ober, see below for more info.

Keep reading...if you dare!

HALLOWEEN IN GALWAY

Did you know that Irish households once left food outside at Halloween to w=
elcome the spirits of their ancestors and keep unwanted spirits away?

Halloween has a rich history in Ireland, so why not grab your friends, expl=
ore Galway and make the most of the spooky season!

Fancy a fright?  The Haunted Walking Tour of Galway City [https://www.galw=
aytourism.ie/haunted-walking-tour-of-galway-city/] explores the city=E2=80=99=
s darker past through scary stories and local legends that bring its histor=
y to life.

From spooky stories to spectacular sights,  Time by Luxmuralis [https://th=
t.ticketsolve.com/ticketbooth/shows/1173668978] brings impressive light and=
 sound displays to St Nicholas=E2=80=99 Collegiate Church.

The fun doesn't stop there!  See what else is happening in Galway this Hall=
oween.  [https://www.galwaytourism.ie/event/galway-aboo-halloween-festival=
/]

GET CREATIVE AT MAKERSPACE

Want to try something new or bring an idea to life?  MakerSpace [https://l=
ibrary.universityofgalway.ie/studying/makerspace/], located on the ground f=
loor of the Library, is a space where you can get creative, develop ideas a=
nd collaborate with others. No booking is required!

From free  3D printing [https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pages/ResponsePage.a=
spx?id=3DhrHjE0bEq0qcbZq5u3aBbKnA84xtP6VKpjjlToM7g-dURFNORVdPQTZRTzI5Uk5KS0=
RMS0oyREZBUy4u] and laser cutting to sewing machines and drones, there are =
plenty of ways to explore the equipment, get involved in existing projects =
and bring your own designs to life!

If you are interested in volunteering or want to find out more, email the M=
akerSpace team at  [libmakerspace@universityofgalway.ie].

GET COOKING THIS AUTUMN

As October brings cooler weather and darker evenings, it=E2=80=99s a lovely=
 time to get creative in the kitchen and explore seasonal ingredients. Cook=
ing at home is a great way to enjoy fresh food, try something different and=
 make the most of seasonal produce.

Why give cooking at home a go?

Save money: Cooking at home is cheaper than relying on takeaways or eating =
out.

Make nutritious choices: Include a variety of ingredients and build balance=
d meals.

Learn new skills: Try new techniques and build your confidence.

Unwind and get creative: Cooking can be relaxing and fun, get experimental =
with ingredients and recipes.

Connect with others: Cook with friends, share meals and enjoy spending time=
 together.

An Bhialann has shared some seasonal recipes, along with tips on food, nutr=
ition and harvest traditions.  Check out the full guide [https://nuigalway=
ie-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/g/personal/0129727s_universityofgalway_ie/IQCncjnz=
_yrRQKXz04Wco5p8Ad3Y_-6XntbhU4VfPFdxOLw?e=3DZ6K5v1]!

SPACE FOR EVERYONE

Black History Month is a time to celebrate the culture and achievements of =
Black communities, while learning more about Black history and experiences.

We want every student to feel valued, included and welcomed at our Universi=
ty. Our Race Equality Advisors offer a safe space for students to receive s=
upport, guidance and advice. To book a confidential meeting, visit  their w=
ebpage [https://www.universityofgalway.ie/equalityanddiversity/raceequalit=
y/meettheteam/] or email  [raceequality@universityofgalway.ie].

Check out the events section below for details of the Black History Month E=
xhibition.

IMEACHTA=C3=8D - EVENTS

Computer Skills Workshop

When: 6pm, Wednesday 28 October

Where: CSB-1007

Workshop on computer skills that are useful to have for students in physics=
 and other scientific disciplines.

Bring your laptop, follow along and ask as many questions as your heart des=
ires. Free pizza afterwards!

What Do Engineers Do?

When: 6pm, Wednesday 28 October

Where: ENG-G018, Alice Perry building

Curious about what life as an engineer actually looks like? Join the  IEEE =
student branch [https://socs.universityofgalway.ie/societies/ieeestudentbr=
anch] and Vincent Walsh and Keith Hynes from Microchip Technology, for a gl=
impse into the day-to-day life of an engineer and what working in the field=
 is really like.

Everyone=E2=80=99s welcome, so come along, hear what they have to say and s=
tick around for the Q&A at the end!

Pub Quiz

When: 7:15pm, Wednesday 28 October

Where: Busker Brownes, Cross Street

Join the Video Game Society Pub Quiz on all things video games! Prizes on t=
he night! Tickets =E2=82=AC5 per person: Maximum of 6 Teams: 4-6 People Max=
 Costumes welcome but not mandatory!

Celebrating Black History Month

When: 11am-2pm, Thursday 29 October

Where: The Hub, =C3=81ras na Mac L=C3=A9inn

Explore an exhibition hosted with the help of the  African Caribbean Societ=
y [https://socs.universityofgalway.ie/societies/africancaribbeansociety] h=
onouring Black contributions through colonial histories, literature, cultur=
e, identity and the generations shaping our future.

The Mayor of Galway, Councillor Helen Ogbu, will officially open this event=
=2E

Drop in, discover powerful stories, and celebrate Black legacies in Ireland=
 and beyond.

2016-oween Halloween Party

When: 8pm, Thursday 29 October

Where: Sult

Join the Students' Union as they travel back in time to 2016 for their 2016=
Oween Halloween Party.

There are prizes to be won for the best fancy dress and it=E2=80=99s free e=
ntry!

Keep up to date on events in the Student Calendar [https://socs.university=
ofgalway.ie/events/]

AN RAIBH A FHIOS AGAT?

Fees Deadline

The fees payment deadline for semester one is Saturday 31 October.  All stu=
dents who remain registered beyond this date will be liable for full fees f=
or semester one.  Any withdrawals after this date may impact current or fut=
ure funding opportunities. A late payment penalty of =E2=82=AC200 applies w=
here fees are paid after the deadline. Find out more on the Fees Office  we=
bsite [https://www.universityofgalway.ie/student-fees/].

Marie Birkett Bursary

This bursary will support a first-year undergraduate student at University =
of Galway with care experience or kinship care experience. The bursary has =
a total value of =E2=82=AC6,000, paid in equal annual instalments throughou=
t an undergraduate degree.

Applications close 6 November 2026.  Learn more & apply.  [https://univers=
ityofgalway.ie/access/scholarshipsfunds/mariebirkettbursary/]

Galway Wind Park scholarship

This scholarship offers students living within 15km of the Galway Wind Park=
 an opportunity to apply for 50% funding support towards third-level educat=
ion fees up to a maximum of 3 years. Check  their website [https://www.uni=
versityofgalway.ie/undergraduate-scholarships/galwaywindparkscholarship/] f=
or more info.

Take a look at the new  Scholarships webpage [https://www.universityofgalw=
ay.ie/scholarships/] to see all the available scholarships for students, bo=
th undergrads and postgrads.

Sustainability Fund for Student Societies

Do you have an idea for a sustainability event on campus? The Sustainabilit=
y Office is offering =E2=82=AC500 awards to support student societies to br=
ing sustainability event ideas to life on campus during 2026=E2=80=9327.

Applications close Friday 6 November. Find out more on  their website. [ht=
tps://www.universityofgalway.ie/sustainability/studentsresources/societiess=
ustainabilityfund/]

TACA=C3=8DOCHTA=C3=8D - SUPPORTS

Need support? Find information on the resources available by clicking on th=
e  Support Wheel link [https://www.universityofgalway.ie/student-services/=
supportwheel/].

We want your feedback!

If you have suggestions for future editions of the weekly Student Enquiry C=
entre ezine, please get in touch by emailing  [sec@universityofgalway.ie].

